## HF-001 — Remote Authentication Followed by PowerShell

### Finding

```text
Remote network authentication was followed by PowerShell execution
on the target Windows endpoint.
```

### Systems

```text
Source:
WIN11-01

Target:
WIN11-02
```

### Associated Telemetry

```text
Event ID 4624
Logon Type 3

Event ID 4104
PowerShell Script Block Logging
```

### Disposition

```text
Authorized Security Simulation
```

---

## Finding Analysis

The individual behaviors do not independently establish compromise.

### Network Authentication

```text
4624 + Logon Type 3
```

establishes successful network authentication.

It does not independently establish malicious lateral movement.

### PowerShell

```text
4104
```

provides visibility into PowerShell execution.

PowerShell itself is a legitimate Windows administration technology.

### Combined Context

The relationship:

```text
Remote Network Authentication
        |
        v
PowerShell Execution
```

provides more investigative value than either event evaluated independently.

